WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.400
Welcome to Grade 3 English, Unit 4: Places and Community.

2
00:00:05.020 --> 00:00:09.480
In this unit you will explore the places in
your community and the people who help you there.

3
00:00:10.100 --> 00:00:14.620
You will learn to name places like the hospital,
the market, the court, the college and the garden,

4
00:00:14.940 --> 00:00:18.660
and to talk about helpers like the
doctor, the officer and the sailor.

5
00:00:19.220 --> 00:00:26.020
You will describe places using words like quiet and busy,
give clear instructions, ask questions with do and does,

6
00:00:26.520 --> 00:00:28.620
and explain your ideas with the word “because”.

7
00:00:29.420 --> 00:00:33.660
By the end, you will be ready to write your
own report about a place in your community —

8
00:00:33.980 --> 00:00:36.160
just like Amal does in this unit's story.

9
00:00:36.740 --> 00:00:41.860
In this short lecture, preview the key
ideas and prepare for the independent lesson.

10
00:00:42.560 --> 00:00:47.460
By the end of this unit, you will be able to name
places in your community and the people who work there.

11
00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:52.440
You will also describe a place using
adjectives and opposites, like quiet and busy.

12
00:00:53.020 --> 00:00:57.440
You will also give simple instructions
using imperatives (“Exit the court quietly.”)

13
00:00:58.060 --> 00:01:00.140
Keep these goals in mind as you work.

14
00:01:00.660 --> 00:01:06.140
Your vocabulary work begins with these words:
noise, choice, enjoy, annoy, job, beneath.

15
00:01:06.980 --> 00:01:11.120
Listen to each word, look at what it means,
and try to use it when you talk and write.

16
00:01:11.780 --> 00:01:16.120
The reading sequence includes Our
Community and A Poem: “Places I Know”.

17
00:01:16.880 --> 00:01:21.580
Read slowly, look at the pictures,
and find the big idea in each text.

18
00:01:22.060 --> 00:01:25.580
When you answer a question, point to the words that show it.

19
00:01:26.440 --> 00:01:30.400
The first language focus is Imperatives (Giving Instructions).

20
00:01:31.240 --> 00:01:35.380
An imperative is a special way to use a
verb to give a command or an instruction.

21
00:01:35.980 --> 00:01:37.480
It tells someone to do something.

22
00:01:38.140 --> 00:01:44.740
We need imperatives to give clear directions, like “Exit
the court quietly” or “Go to the hospital if you are sick.”

23
00:01:45.640 --> 00:01:48.840
Look at the examples, then try
the pattern in your own sentences.

24
00:01:50.020 --> 00:01:54.160
In speaking, you will complete Speaking 1 — My Community.

25
00:01:54.760 --> 00:01:57.680
Say your ideas clearly and listen to your partner.

26
00:01:58.360 --> 00:02:03.520
In writing, you will draw, trace, copy or write,
then check your work with a grown-up or the AI tutor.

27
00:02:04.120 --> 00:02:05.140
You are ready to begin.

28
00:02:05.660 --> 00:02:10.160
Start with the words, then the reading and the
questions, then the grammar, speaking and writing.

29
00:02:10.980 --> 00:02:15.740
Ask the AI tutor for help any time, and bring your
questions to a live session too if you join one.
